# StudioDesk frontend

Canon wins. Workspace rules: `studio-desk-docs/.cursor/rules/00-workspace-core.mdc`.

- Main branch: `development`.
- Before claiming the slice done, run and pass in this repo: `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm lint` (`oxlint --type-aware`), `pnpm format:check`, and `pnpm test`.
- CI on every push runs `pnpm lint` and `pnpm format:check` before `pnpm test`. If either fails, the job stops and the server is not updated. `pnpm test` alone does not catch them.
- On 2026-10-08 `pnpm lint` failed on `String(response.body)` in a test. `body` is not always a string; `String` on an object becomes `[object Object]`. Read it only when it is a string.
- The same lint failed on `setState` called directly inside `useEffect` (`react(set-state-in-effect)`). That starts another render from the effect. Set state from the finished request, or defer it. Do not call it synchronously in the effect.
- `pnpm format:check` then failed because new test files were not formatted. Run `pnpm exec prettier --write` on files you added or edited.
